<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is a laning conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A laning conveyor distributes a single-file stream of product across multiple parallel lanes. Product enters on one lane and exits on two, three, four, or more lanes. Laning conveyors feed case packers, <a href="/conveyor-functions/tray-loading/">tray loaders</a>, and cartoners that require product arranged in rows.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What is chicaning on a conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Chicaning (serpentine routing) lanes product through S-shaped guide rails. Product enters single-file, contacts the first angled rail, and diverts to lane one. When lane one fills, a gate sends the next products past to lane two, and so on. Chicaning works best for round containers (bottles, cans, jars) that roll smoothly against guide rails.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">What is the difference between collating and laning?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Laning divides one product stream into multiple parallel lanes. Collating arranges products within those lanes into a specific pattern, a 3×4 array, a 2×5 group, for case packing. Laning happens first (one stream becomes many lanes). Collating happens second (many lanes form a count pattern). Both functions often occur on the same conveyor section.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What throughput can a laning conveyor handle?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Throughput depends on the laning method. Chicane systems handle 200–600+ bottles per minute. Servo lane-select diverters handle 50–200+ packages per minute. Speed-differential systems handle 50–200 products per minute. Delta robots handle 80–200 picks per minute per robot. The throughput math: infeed rate divided by number of lanes equals per-lane rate.</p>

